\begin{Verbatim}[commandchars=\\\{\}]
    \PYGZsh{} Markdown Syntax Guide

This document provides examples of basic Markdown syntax elements, including headings, lists, links, images, tables, and code blocks.

\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}\PYGZhy{}

\PYG{g+gu}{\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{} Headings}

Use \PYG{l+s+sb}{`\PYGZsh{}`} for main headings, \PYG{l+s+sb}{`\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{}`} for sub\PYGZhy{}headings, and so on.

\PYG{g+gh}{\PYGZsh{} Main Heading (H1)}
\PYG{g+gu}{\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{} Subheading (H2)}
\PYG{g+gu}{\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{} Sub\PYGZhy{}subheading (H3)}

\PYG{g+gu}{\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{} Emphasis}

\PYG{k}{\PYGZhy{}}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{g+ge}{*Italic*}: \PYG{l+s+sb}{`*Italic*`} or \PYG{l+s+sb}{`\PYGZus{}Italic\PYGZus{}`}
\PYG{k}{\PYGZhy{}}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{g+gs}{**Bold**}: \PYG{l+s+sb}{`**Bold**`} or \PYG{l+s+sb}{`\PYGZus{}\PYGZus{}Bold\PYGZus{}\PYGZus{}`}
\PYG{k}{\PYGZhy{}}\PYG{+w}{ }***Bold and Italic***: \PYG{l+s+sb}{`***Bold and Italic***`}

\PYG{g+gu}{\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{} Lists}

\PYG{g+gu}{\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{} Unordered List}

\PYG{k}{\PYGZhy{}}\PYG{+w}{ }Item 1
\PYG{k}{\PYGZhy{}}\PYG{+w}{ }Item 2
\PYG{+w}{  }\PYG{k}{\PYGZhy{}}\PYG{+w}{ }Subitem 2.1
\PYG{+w}{  }\PYG{k}{\PYGZhy{}}\PYG{+w}{ }Subitem 2.2

\PYG{g+gu}{\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{} Ordered List}

\PYG{k}{1.} First item
\PYG{k}{2.} Second item
\PYG{+w}{   }\PYG{k}{1.} Subitem 2.1
\PYG{+w}{   }\PYG{k}{2.} Subitem 2.2

\PYG{g+gu}{\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{} Links and Images}

\PYG{g+gu}{\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{} Link}

[\PYG{n+nt}{OpenAI Website}](\PYG{n+na}{https://www.openai.com})

\PYG{g+gu}{\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{} Image}

![\PYG{n+nt}{OpenAI Logo}](\PYG{n+na}{https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/62/OpenAI\PYGZus{}Logo.svg})

\PYG{g+gu}{\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{} Blockquotes}

Use \PYG{l+s+sb}{`\PYGZgt{}`} to create a blockquote.

\PYG{k}{\PYGZgt{} }\PYG{g+ge}{\PYGZdq{}Artificial intelligence is the future, and the future is now.\PYGZdq{} \PYGZhy{} Author Unknown}

\PYG{g+gu}{\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{} Code Blocks and Inline Code}

\PYG{g+gu}{\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{} Inline Code}

Use backticks to indicate inline code, like \PYG{l+s+sb}{`print(\PYGZdq{}Hello, World!\PYGZdq{})`}.

\PYG{g+gu}{\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{}\PYGZsh{} Code Block}

```python
def greet():
    print(\PYGZdq{}Hello, World!\PYGZdq{})

\end{Verbatim}
